            <fr:title text="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference">(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(*): for every proper <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-stable irreducible subvariety
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex> of a nilpotent orbit <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {O}_{\lambda }]]></fr:tex>, the isotropy bound holds —
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  W \le  \frac {1}{2} \dim  \mathcal {O}_{\lambda }]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> After <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0016/" title="(H1): the incidence theorem for flagless pencils" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0016/" display-uri="ffi-0016" type="local">(H1)</fr:link> this is the single remaining geometric
statement between the program and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">the height conjecture</fr:link>.
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">Orbital varieties are Lagrangian</fr:link> supplies it whenever <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex>
is an orbital variety; what is left is the case of subvarieties carrying
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\ge  2]]></fr:tex> moduli of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-orbits, where characteristic <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[p]]></fr:tex> denies
the generic-smoothness argument. First possible at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 6]]></fr:tex>, which is
why the ladder <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0018/" title="Height at n ≤ 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0018/" display-uri="ffi-0018" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex></fr:link> has to be climbed by
hand.</html:p>
            <html:p>The infinitesimal form of the same statement is <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0050/" title="(W): the wall conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0050/" display-uri="ffi-0050" type="local">(W)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">Orbital varieties are Lagrangian</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0016/" title="(H1): the incidence theorem for flagless pencils" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0016/" display-uri="ffi-0016" type="local">(H1): the incidence theorem for flagless pencils</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: distilled.tex Part 3; journal sec:h1 and the pass 6--8
apparatus.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0009</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0009/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The height conjecture">The height conjecture</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> and every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {ht} J = \frac {n(n+1)}{2},
  \qquad  \text {equivalently} \qquad 
  \dim  V(J) = \frac {n(n - 1)}{2}:
]]></fr:tex>
the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\frac {n(n+1)}{2}]]></fr:tex> invariants <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}^{i}(c_{j})]]></fr:tex>,
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[0 \le  i < j \le  n]]></fr:tex>, form a regular sequence in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[S]]></fr:tex> and extend to a
homogeneous system of parameters. The conjectured dimension is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  \mathrm {Fl}]]></fr:tex> — up to dimension, the
flag witnesses must be everything.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Proven for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex> every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>
(<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0019/" title="Height at n ≤ 5" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0019/" display-uri="ffi-0019" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex></fr:link>); for characteristic <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[0]]></fr:tex>, every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>;
for all but finitely many characteristics per <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>, ineffectively; and
for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex> every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex> (<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0018/" title="Height at n ≤ 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0018/" display-uri="ffi-0018" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex></fr:link>). Open in
general, and what is open is exactly <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0005/" title="The Steenrod ideal" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0005/" display-uri="ffi-0005" type="local">The Steenrod ideal</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0008/" title="The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0008/" display-uri="ffi-0008" type="local">The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: distilled.tex Part 1; journal thm:height-n7, thm:m8,
cor:height-n8, cor:height-n9.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-height/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sec-height</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/sec-height/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest › The height ladder"><fr:link href="/ffi/index/" title="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/index/" display-uri="index" type="local">finite-field-invariants: a reference forest</fr:link> › The height ladder</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>The conjecture is a theorem for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex>. Each rung is a
  different mechanism, and the reductions that carry rungs 8 and 9 are
  worth more than the rungs.</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0018/" title="Height at n ≤ 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0018/" display-uri="ffi-0018" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the milestone.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0019/" title="Height at n ≤ 5" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0019/" display-uri="ffi-0019" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — finitely many orbits.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0020/" title="Height at n ≤ 7" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0020/" display-uri="ffi-0020" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  7]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the modality theorem,
    unconditional.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0021/" title="(M8): the per-cell modality reduction at n = 8" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0021/" display-uri="ffi-0021" type="local">(M8)</fr:link> — the address reduction at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0022/" title="Height at n = 8" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0022/" display-uri="ffi-0022" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — pseudo-Levi collapse and the
    torus defect.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S)</fr:link> — the reduction at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0024/" title="(S+): the ledger conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0024/" display-uri="ffi-0024" type="local">(S+)</fr:link> — the ledger that would close it.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0025/" title="Height at n = 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0025/" display-uri="ffi-0025" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the cascade.</html:li></html:ul>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
