        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0019/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0019</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0019/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Height at n ≤ 5">Height at n ≤ 5</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> holds for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex> and
every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex> the Borel has finitely many orbits on the
nilradical (Kashiarov; Hille--Röhrle), so <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> is not
needed: the isotropy bound of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">the orbital-variety theorem</fr:link>,
plus at most one modulus of orbits, covers every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-stable
irreducible subvariety.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">Orbital varieties are Lagrangian</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal sec:small-n; Kashiarov, Hille--Röhrle for the
finiteness input.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0020/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0020</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0020/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Height at n ≤ 7">Height at n ≤ 7</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>theorem</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> holds for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  7]]></fr:tex> and
every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>, unconditionally.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> The modality theorem: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {mod}(B : \mathfrak {n}_{n}) = 1]]></fr:tex> for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 6, 7]]></fr:tex>. With
at most one modulus of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-orbits on the nilradical, the
two-moduli case of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> never arises, so
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">the orbital-variety theorem</fr:link> closes every subvariety. The
modality inputs are published rows discharged against machine
certificates (Goddard--Goodwin; GMR2).</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">Orbital varieties are Lagrangian</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0027/" title="Borel modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0027/" display-uri="ffi-0027" type="local">Borel modality</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: journal thm:height-n7 (fourteenth pass); census 275/276/277
plus the diamond; verified against Goddard--Goodwin and GMR2.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0009</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0009/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The height conjecture">The height conjecture</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="area">height</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> and every prime power <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {ht} J = \frac {n(n+1)}{2},
  \qquad  \text {equivalently} \qquad 
  \dim  V(J) = \frac {n(n - 1)}{2}:
]]></fr:tex>
the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\frac {n(n+1)}{2}]]></fr:tex> invariants <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}^{i}(c_{j})]]></fr:tex>,
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[0 \le  i < j \le  n]]></fr:tex>, form a regular sequence in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[S]]></fr:tex> and extend to a
homogeneous system of parameters. The conjectured dimension is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  \mathrm {Fl}]]></fr:tex> — up to dimension, the
flag witnesses must be everything.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Proven for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex> every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>
(<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0019/" title="Height at n ≤ 5" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0019/" display-uri="ffi-0019" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex></fr:link>); for characteristic <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[0]]></fr:tex>, every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>;
for all but finitely many characteristics per <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>, ineffectively; and
for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex> every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex> (<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0018/" title="Height at n ≤ 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0018/" display-uri="ffi-0018" type="local">height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex></fr:link>). Open in
general, and what is open is exactly <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0005/" title="The Steenrod ideal" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0005/" display-uri="ffi-0005" type="local">The Steenrod ideal</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0008/" title="The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0008/" display-uri="ffi-0008" type="local">The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
              <html:em>Provenance: distilled.tex Part 1; journal thm:height-n7, thm:m8,
cor:height-n8, cor:height-n9.</html:em>
            </html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
